# No input at all — synthwave has no model: the whole scene is a pure function
# of time. The script exists because `--capture-at-frame N` (the only
# frame-indexed, byte-reproducible capture trigger) requires `--input-script`,
# and `--fixed-time` would pin the clock and freeze the rolling hills. So this
# is the empty scenario, and frames advance by --script-dt alone.
#
# Format: <frame:int> <KeyName> <down|up>; `#` starts a comment.
#
#   functor -d examples/synthwave run native --input-script boxart.script \
#     --script-dt 0.0166667 --capture-at-frame 60 --capture-frame /tmp/sw.png
